# Types and errors

- No empty `catch` / silent swallow. Log or rethrow with context.
- Avoid `any` and unjustified casts (`as`). Prefer proper types or narrow safely.
- User-facing errors ≠ internal stack traces. Return safe messages; log details server-side.
- Prefer a project `logger` over `console` in server/production paths.

```typescript
// BAD
try {
  await save(data);
} catch (e) {}

// GOOD
try {
  await save(data);
} catch (e) {
  logger.error('save failed', { error: e instanceof Error ? e.message : e });
  throw e;
}
```
